A58 — under the FPS limiter, hold a second mailbox commit for the next vblank

A mailbox client that paces itself just under the refresh rate (a guest at
~59.3 fps under a 60 cap on a 59.97 Hz panel) completes two commits inside one
composite window about once a second. The done-commit handling latches every
non-FIFO commit as it completes, so the second one replaces the first before
the paint and the panel repeats a frame (58.3-59.0 fps, 2.7-2.9 % doubled
intervals in gamenative-drm PR #46, B4-B6). The client cannot avoid it: the
latch point is gamescope's vblank wakeup (target vblank minus the rolling
draw-time estimate minus the red zone), which only gamescope knows.

With gn_mailbox_hold on, while the FPS limiter is engaged for a window (a
target FPS is set, the window is not limiter-exempt, no VRR), the done-commit
handling for Xwayland and xdg windows does this for non-FIFO commits:

- the first commit to complete for the coming paint is latched as today;
- a newer one is held in the done list instead of replacing it, and is latched
  by the first done-commit pass of the next vblank cycle (the vblank pass
  always runs one, so a held commit never waits for the client);
- a third replaces the held one; the replaced commit is dropped from the
  window's queue, which releases its buffer and discards its presentation
  feedback, as a mailbox replace does today.

The queue is one deep, the client is never blocked, and a window that delivers
at or below the refresh rate never loses a frame. A held commit's earliest
present time is stamped by the pass that latches it. FIFO commits, unlimited
windows and VRR are unchanged.

A held commit is shown one paint late. A client that keeps delivering one
commit per vblank never drains that: each new commit finds its paint taken by
the carried one and is carried in turn, a standing one-frame delay (seen with
in-game VSync on, where every commit was carried). So the carry is bounded:
after gn_mailbox_hold_max_carry paints in a row (default 8) have shown a
carried commit, the next fresh commit is latched at once and replaces the
carried one, a mailbox replace that drops one frame and puts the window back
on its own paint. A client below the refresh rate drains the carry by itself
at its next gap, as before.

gn_mailbox_hold: -1 (default) = on when the gamenative-drm backend is in use
(GAMENATIVE_DRM_SOCKET set), else off; gamescope_gn_mailbox_hold=0/1 overrides
it; on Android the property debug.gamescope.gn_mailbox_hold=0/1 wins when set.
gn_mailbox_hold_max_carry (0 = unbounded) follows the same pattern, with the
property debug.gamescope.gn_mailbox_hold_max_carry. Both are resolved once, at
the first done-commit pass.

Logs: "gn_mailbox_hold=<0|1> source=<default|env|prop> max_carry=N" once at
start, and about every 600 vblanks while the hold does anything:
"gn_mailbox_hold: deferred=N carried_paints=C max_run=R collapsed=X
replaced=M over K vblanks". deferred counts each held commit once;
carried_paints counts paints that showed a commit one paint late (the latency
the hold adds); max_run is the longest run of those; collapsed counts carries
ended by the bound; replaced counts held commits dropped for a newer one.

